  "description": "The splice of set_scalar is computed on code points, never on UTF-16 code units or on normalized text. U+1F600 and U+1F601 share their high surrogate and U+1F600 and U+1FA00 their low surrogate: a prefix or suffix counted in code units would cut a character in half. 'e' + U+0301 and U+00E9 are different strings: both code points are replaced. Each case has a concurrent insert next to the replaced character, which lands where it would only if the splice is exactly (index, delete, insert) as R23 gives it. splice_text takes integers and a string.",
